# OpenClaw boundary

OpenClaw is **config authority**. DragonClaw orchestrates; it does not invent schema rules.

## Always use OC CLI for

- `openclaw config validate` before apply
- `openclaw doctor` / `--fix` during troubleshoot (LLM interprets output)
- `openclaw models list`, `models status` for model probes (fallback catalog)
- `openclaw onboard --non-interactive` for API-key provider auth when catalog supports it
- `openclaw models set` after DC model pick (validate-gated)
- Interactive configure/channel flows via **TTY handoff** (`oc_interactive`) — deferred for model/provider; future channels/OAuth

## DragonClaw owns

- `dragonclaw` entry, install bootstrap, session/checklist
- Menu framing and NL routing to `flow_id`
- **`dc_catalog`** live model lists (adapter classes) + `dc_menu` model pick
- Local secret inspection for diagnosis (with user consent)
- Validate-gated minimal patches and backups
- Plain-English explanation of OC tool output

## Non-interactive vs interactive

- `subprocess.run(capture_output=True)` — tools only (`oc_json`, doctor, validate)
- Foreground PTY — user-facing OC wizards (`oc_interactive`); resume agent when subprocess exits

## Failure handling

On validate or probe failure: feed error to LLM, retry with tools — do not emit another guessed full config.
